  [1mClassification: architectural.[0m "Logging" is a new subsystem — there's no existing logging flow here to modify, just
  scattered [38;5;153mconsole.log[39m calls. It carries real design choices (structured vs. plain, levels, transport, redaction) and
  the shape you pick becomes an interface every future call site depends on. So I'll work through questions → approaches
  → a design → a written spec, rather than just dropping a logger in.

  One thing I want to flag up front, since it shapes the design rather than being a detail: [38;5;153mapp.js:5[39m already logs the
  username on every login attempt, and [38;5;153mpassword[39m is in scope at the same call sites. Any logging we add around that form
  is one careless line away from putting credentials into production logs. I'll treat redaction as a first-class
  requirement in the design, not an afterthought.

